@* Plan A22 (pass 26): an AFV crew buttoning up or exposing itself (D5.33), in its side's MPh or APh; the page lists the AFVs that may change, read for the
   view, and proposes the change. *@
<ActionSection Title="Crew exposure" Key="crew-exposure">
<RuleHelp Id="bu-help" Summary="An open-topped AFV's owner places or removes its BU counter once in its MPh or APh, not after it Prep Fired nor while its crew is Stunned; a CE crew may fire the AAMG and is Vulnerable to Collateral Attacks (D5.33, D5.34, D5.3).">
    The owner of an open-topped AFV places or removes its BU counter in its own MPh or APh, once per phase, not in an MPh after it Prep
    Fired, and not while its crew is Stunned (D5.33, D5.34). A CE crew may fire the AAMG and is Vulnerable to Collateral Attacks (D5.3, D.8B).
</RuleHelp>
<div class="toolbar">
    @foreach (var afv in Vehicles)
    {
        <button class="bu-toggle" data-vehicle="@afv.Id" @onclick="@(() => OnToggle.InvokeAsync(afv))">Propose: @afv.Id @(afv.ButtonedUp ? "exposes its crew (CE)" : "buttons up (BU)")</button>
    }
</div>
</ActionSection>

@code {
    /// <summary>An AFV that may change its crew's exposure, and whether it is BU now.</summary>
    public sealed record Exposure(string Id, bool ButtonedUp);

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<Exposure> Vehicles { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Exposure> OnToggle { get; set; }
}
